# S8 — lesson-modules-view (ai-tutor), census docs/PICT_CENSUS.md § S8.
# See tests/models/lesson-modules-view.oracle.ts for the oracle spec.
#
# Drift contract: `hasElevatedAccess = isAdmin || isInstructor || isTa || isUnitAdmin`
# is written independently in routes/activities.js (GET /lessons/:id/activities)
# and routes/modules.js (GET /courses/:id/modules) — same formula today, but
# nothing stops it drifting. `Role` collapses the five underlying booleans
# (isAdmin/isInstructor/isTa/isUnitAdmin/isStudent) into one dimension since
# they are mutually exclusive in the world-builder (one seeded user has
# exactly one relationship to the course). Both routes are exercised for
# every row in the world-builder (apps/extensions/ai-tutor/server/tests/integration/lesson-modules-view.pict.test.js)
# rather than making the route a PICT factor — same reasoning as `Path` in
# tests/models/material-visibility.pict.
Role:       ADMIN, INSTRUCTOR, TA, UNIT_ADMIN, STUDENT, NONE, ANON
Published:  yes, no
Found:      yes, no

IF [Role] = "ANON" THEN [Found] = "yes";
